And as we understand,
calendaring and other stuff

00:11:22.970 --> 00:11:25.280
were that way five years ago.

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:29.140
So as the work is
transforming, Smartsheet

00:11:29.140 --> 00:11:32.020
provides 18,000 new
processes or projects

00:11:32.020 --> 00:11:33.790
to their users every day.

00:11:33.790 --> 00:11:35.322
So it's a growing
world where people

00:11:35.322 --> 00:11:37.030
realize that they
don't have a tool to do

00:11:37.030 --> 00:11:39.130
the things they need to do.

00:11:39.130 --> 00:11:43.120
So what we are is
collaborative work management.

00:11:43.120 --> 00:11:47.260
Collaborative work management
basically comes to this place

00:11:47.260 --> 00:11:50.410
where we had project management
software in the past,

00:11:50.410 --> 00:11:53.020
but we were really using
Excel, or spreadsheets,

00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:55.600
and email to solve a
problem which was, I

00:11:55.600 --> 00:11:56.940
got to gather data from people.

00:11:56.940 --> 00:11:57.790
We got to talk about it.

00:11:57.790 --> 00:11:58.581
We got to share it.

00:11:58.581 --> 00:12:00.035
We got to go through it.

00:12:00.035 --> 00:12:01.660
But then we didn't
do anything with it.

00:12:01.660 --> 00:12:03.517
We sort of were
dead-ended there.

00:12:03.517 --> 00:12:05.600
And now the number of apps
where that's happening,

00:12:05.600 --> 00:12:08.880
whether it's sort of legacy
IT apps or other apps

00:12:08.880 --> 00:12:11.690
that people are using,
is increasing in volume.

00:12:11.690 --> 00:12:14.270
And then the number of places
that they are connecting,

00:12:14.270 --> 00:12:16.880
whether that's all
through G Suite or 100

00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:19.400
other products that
are all best of breed,

00:12:19.400 --> 00:12:20.365
is increasing as well.

00:12:20.365 --> 00:12:21.740
So the number of
vectors that you

00:12:21.740 --> 00:12:25.970
have to cover for all of your
users is going up as well.

00:12:25.970 --> 00:12:28.610
And so as we look at
this place-- and this

00:12:28.610 --> 00:12:31.220
is happening now because
users are doing more stuff all

00:12:31.220 --> 00:12:32.060
the time online.

00:12:32.060 --> 00:12:33.740
The velocity is going up.

00:12:33.740 --> 00:12:36.380
So we're living in a world
where these three V's

00:12:36.380 --> 00:12:40.550
are causing us, as
administrators or as developers

00:12:40.550 --> 00:12:43.820
or whichever audience we're
in, to have to deal with this.

00:12:43.820 --> 00:12:46.850
But in order for our users
to be delighted and actually

00:12:46.850 --> 00:12:48.740
want to come to
work every day, we

00:12:48.740 --> 00:12:50.740
have to provide them
with great tools.

00:12:50.740 --> 00:12:53.160
And the great tools
have to work together.

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:55.886
So these are some of our stats
over the Google partnership

00:12:55.886 --> 00:12:57.260
that we've had,
and we've enjoyed

00:12:57.260 --> 00:13:01.499
a really strong partnership with
them for the last four years.

00:13:01.499 --> 00:13:03.290
But I want to talk a
little more about what

00:13:03.290 --> 00:13:04.248
the important thing is.

00:13:04.248 --> 00:13:06.230
So Anand talked
about picking an app.

00:13:06.230 --> 00:13:08.895
And so when you go to pick an
app in the modern workforce,

00:13:08.895 --> 00:13:10.520
we really believe
that you need to pick

00:13:10.520 --> 00:13:13.530
something that's usable by
all teams in the company.

00:13:13.530 --> 00:13:16.340
So it's not enough to just
deploy a project management

00:13:16.340 --> 00:13:18.380
solution and hope your
five project managers can

00:13:18.380 --> 00:13:20.360
cover your 200-person company.

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:22.220
You have to cross boundaries.

00:13:22.220 --> 00:13:24.560
You have to be able to share
internally and externally.

00:13:24.560 --> 00:13:26.450
You have to integrate
all key apps.

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:28.100
And everybody has
to be satisfied.

00:13:28.100 --> 00:13:30.140
That means security
needs to be there.

00:13:30.140 --> 00:13:32.100
That means your control
needs to be there.

00:13:32.100 --> 00:13:34.940
But at the same time, you
really have to show users

00:13:34.940 --> 00:13:37.040
that they have a product
they can use every day,

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:40.146
so that you empower
them to be better.

00:13:40.146 --> 00:13:42.770
So what I wanted to do before I
talked any more, because people

00:13:42.770 --> 00:13:45.186
are like, what's Smartsheet
and what's project management?

00:13:45.186 --> 00:13:48.754
We put together a little video
about how we work with G Suite,

00:13:48.754 --> 00:13:51.170
so you guys could kind of see
a real-world example that we

00:13:51.170 --> 00:13:54.494
do for our users every day.

