00:16:15.310 --> 00:16:17.500
was that Smartsheet was
behind the scenes driving

00:16:17.500 --> 00:16:21.830
some of the work automation
and work management.

00:16:21.830 --> 00:16:24.080
So to that end, I
wanted to talk about how

00:16:24.080 --> 00:16:25.460
we think about this space.

00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:28.130
So traditionally,
project management

00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:30.276
has been sort of to
the single person.

00:16:30.276 --> 00:16:32.150
And as we look at process
management and work

00:16:32.150 --> 00:16:33.525
automation and
the things that we

00:16:33.525 --> 00:16:36.050
used to always do by
emailing around spreadsheets,

00:16:36.050 --> 00:16:38.270
there's a bunch of things
that we can make better,

00:16:38.270 --> 00:16:40.160
and that's by doing
better tracking.

00:16:40.160 --> 00:16:44.390
And so today we have that with
Gmail for our contact lists.

00:16:44.390 --> 00:16:48.080
We can start a Hangout
directly from Smartsheet.

00:16:48.080 --> 00:16:49.820
We can report better,
so we can actually

00:16:49.820 --> 00:16:52.850
merge info from Smartsheet
to power a mail merge

00:16:52.850 --> 00:16:54.354
in Docs for a small business.

00:16:54.354 --> 00:16:55.770
So if you have
somebody that says,

00:16:55.770 --> 00:16:56.936
hey, I have an address list.

00:16:56.936 --> 00:16:58.210
It's in a spreadsheet.

00:16:58.210 --> 00:17:01.137
Import it from Sheets, use
the mail merge functionality,

00:17:01.137 --> 00:17:02.720
and you generate a
bunch of documents.

00:17:02.720 --> 00:17:06.140
It's a fairly simple integration
that can be done every day.

00:17:06.140 --> 00:17:09.050
Then, on the automation front,
we can bring data directly

00:17:09.050 --> 00:17:10.550
from Sheets into
Smartsheet, and we

00:17:10.550 --> 00:17:12.260
can send updated
requests via Gmail

00:17:12.260 --> 00:17:13.819
and fill them out in a form.

00:17:13.819 --> 00:17:15.890
We also do single sign-on.

00:17:15.890 --> 00:17:19.130
We're working right now on skim,
so you can do user provisioning

00:17:19.130 --> 00:17:21.089
and deprovisioning
directly from Google.

00:17:21.089 --> 00:17:23.630
And you can create and attach
and view sheets to Google Drive

00:17:23.630 --> 00:17:25.421
and restrict it to
Google Drive so that you

00:17:25.421 --> 00:17:28.850
can get full management
capability throughout the app

00:17:28.850 --> 00:17:31.449
from Google and
using Smartsheet.

00:17:31.449 --> 00:17:32.990
So it becomes a very
easy way for you

00:17:32.990 --> 00:17:34.340
to control the data
that goes in there,

00:17:34.340 --> 00:17:36.380
and you have a lot of
controls for it coming out.

00:17:36.380 --> 00:17:38.755
But at the same time, the
users get a seamless experience

00:17:38.755 --> 00:17:42.220
with both Smartsheet
and working with Google.

00:17:42.220 --> 00:17:44.360
I guess I can go back to--

00:17:44.360 --> 00:17:46.930
So one of the big
customers that we had

00:17:46.930 --> 00:17:49.540
was a sort of former
Microsoft Project customer

00:17:49.540 --> 00:17:51.140
and migrated over to Google.

00:17:51.140 --> 00:17:54.670
And today, they're actually
a large-scale manufacturing

00:17:54.670 --> 00:17:56.690
software business.

00:17:56.690 --> 00:18:00.250
But essentially, they came by
and said, with Google apps,

00:18:00.250 --> 00:18:02.140
with Workday, and
with Smartsheet,

00:18:02.140 --> 00:18:05.510
we have transformed our entire
business from a legacy stack.

00:18:05.510 --> 00:18:07.330
So eliminated
Microsoft Project that

00:18:07.330 --> 00:18:09.130
was a hole in
their marketplace--

00:18:09.130 --> 00:18:12.070
or a hole in their operation
after they flipped over,

00:18:12.070 --> 00:18:13.590
but also to do
other things which

00:18:13.590 --> 00:18:15.654
throughout human resources,
finances, and sales,

00:18:15.654 --> 00:18:17.320
they're using us every
day from employee

00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:20.600
onboarding to actual
tracking of their sales team.

00:18:20.600 --> 00:18:23.422
So it really allows a powerful
work management experience

00:18:23.422 --> 00:18:25.630
throughout the app, but
again, it does all this stuff

00:18:25.630 --> 00:18:27.100
while working with
the Google apps

00:18:27.100 --> 00:18:28.308
that they're using every day.

00:18:28.308 --> 00:18:30.910
So the learning curve gets
smaller and the deployment

00:18:30.910 --> 00:18:33.320
gets easier.

00:18:33.320 --> 00:18:37.850
So as we talk about transforming
work is a very lofty solution,

00:18:37.850 --> 00:18:40.280
one of the things that we've
been talking a lot about

00:18:40.280 --> 00:18:41.780
is that we have to
empower everybody

00:18:41.780 --> 00:18:43.910
to do automation and
do process and get

00:18:43.910 --> 00:18:45.650
to those things on their own.

00:18:45.650 --> 00:18:47.450
And as you guys have
a large user base,

00:18:47.450 --> 00:18:50.000
you have a set of people that
you're supporting every day,

00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:52.160
it's really
important to remember

00:18:52.160 --> 00:18:53.930
that they are not technical.

00:18:53.930 --> 00:18:56.930
And so we're throwing more and
more apps at them every day,

00:18:56.930 --> 00:18:59.720
and every time they have
to learn a new paradigm.

00:18:59.720 --> 00:19:02.300
And that's great when it's
Snapchat and Facebook and it's

00:19:02.300 --> 00:19:03.527
fun to do on your phone.

00:19:03.527 --> 00:19:05.360
It's not great when you
have to come to work

00:19:05.360 --> 00:19:06.980
and you can't get
your work done.

00:19:06.980 --> 00:19:10.020
And so it's really important
that we do that and continue

00:19:10.020 --> 00:19:11.180
to do that.

00:19:11.180 --> 00:19:13.960
We have more intelligence
now today with AI

00:19:13.960 --> 00:19:16.834
and powering those things, so
we should make our apps better.

00:19:16.834 --> 00:19:18.500
And the thing that I
keep telling people

00:19:18.500 --> 00:19:21.560
is we did a user study
recently, and our users

00:19:21.560 --> 00:19:23.900
said, when the word
"if" appeared on screen,

00:19:23.900 --> 00:19:25.970
that it was too programmer-y.

00:19:25.970 --> 00:19:28.524
It was too hard to use the
word "if" in a construct.

00:19:28.524 --> 00:19:29.690
They wanted the word "when."

00:19:29.690 --> 00:19:32.030
And the reason I bring that
up is all these developers,

00:19:32.030 --> 00:19:34.321
and everybody else, is saying,
I can teach these people

00:19:34.321 --> 00:19:35.372
to be citizen developers!

00:19:35.372 --> 00:19:36.830
But I think that's
the wrong thing.

00:19:36.830 --> 00:19:39.540
I think we need to support
them in using lots of apps,

00:19:39.540 --> 00:19:41.900
and I think we need to do
it to make work better.

00:19:41.900 --> 00:19:45.680
So what I'm hoping, and what I'm
hoping more people in the room

00:19:45.680 --> 00:19:48.560
sort of attach to
and build for, is

00:19:48.560 --> 00:19:50.000
let's agree to
delight our users,

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:51.760
whether that's giving
them the apps they want

00:19:51.760 --> 00:19:53.634
or managing the apps so
they don't see what's

00:19:53.634 --> 00:19:55.340
going on behind the scenes.

00:19:55.340 --> 00:19:58.730
Let's get apps to talk together
without copy and paste.

00:19:58.730 --> 00:20:00.920
One of our biggest use
cases for Dashboard

00:20:00.920 --> 00:20:02.660
is the elimination
of PowerPoint,

00:20:02.660 --> 00:20:05.540
because what people want to
see is real-time dashboards

00:20:05.540 --> 00:20:08.360
of projects, and they don't
want to copy and paste them

00:20:08.360 --> 00:20:11.300
out of a spreadsheet that they
roll up, that they put in there

00:20:11.300 --> 00:20:12.674
and spend an hour each week.

00:20:12.674 --> 00:20:14.090
So find the things
that you can do

00:20:14.090 --> 00:20:16.730
to support your users every
day so they can spend less time

00:20:16.730 --> 00:20:18.780
doing those sorts of things.

00:20:18.780 --> 00:20:20.300
And then, find the
things that they

00:20:20.300 --> 00:20:21.800
don't know they don't know.

00:20:21.800 --> 00:20:24.170
So as we talk about all
this artificial intelligence

00:20:24.170 --> 00:20:29.490
and other things that we can
use to support our users,

00:20:29.490 --> 00:20:32.340
let's use AI to make
their life better,

00:20:32.340 --> 00:20:35.872
not let's use our AI to surface
10 times more information.

00:20:35.872 --> 00:20:37.830
And so my challenge to
all of these people that

00:20:37.830 --> 00:20:41.310
are supporting all their
customers every day

00:20:41.310 --> 00:20:44.929
is let's make work
better not because we

00:20:44.929 --> 00:20:46.470
have a lot more
technology, but let's

00:20:46.470 --> 00:20:49.480
make it better so that
people are more effective.

00:20:49.480 --> 00:20:53.180
And so to that end, we've
announced at this conference

00:20:53.180 --> 00:20:56.960
that we are working on
the Hangouts Chat, which

00:20:56.960 --> 00:21:00.440
is the Hangouts v2 to go with
our Hangouts v1 integration.

00:21:00.440 --> 00:21:03.350
We're also looking at Google Now
to make it easier to input data

00:21:03.350 --> 00:21:04.405
into our system.

00:21:04.405 --> 00:21:05.780
And at the same
time, we're going

00:21:05.780 --> 00:21:07.700
to invest heavy in
machine learning,

00:21:07.700 --> 00:21:10.760
not to sort of predict
where people are going,

00:21:10.760 --> 00:21:13.580
but to help them find the
features that they don't have.

00:21:13.580 --> 00:21:16.910
And so as we look forward to
innovation, as we look forward

00:21:16.910 --> 00:21:19.820
to doing more things with
Google and supporting you guys

00:21:19.820 --> 00:21:21.770
and building better
products, we really

00:21:21.770 --> 00:21:23.930
look to making a great
product, but using

00:21:23.930 --> 00:21:26.210
the power of technology
and innovating on the way

00:21:26.210 --> 00:21:28.040
our users can consume it.

00:21:28.040 --> 00:21:30.920
It needs to be much easier for
users to do the hard things

00:21:30.920 --> 00:21:36.560
that we want them to do, so
they can be more effective.

00:21:36.560 --> 00:21:38.940
So if you want to see us,
we'll be down at booth D2.

00:21:38.940 --> 00:21:40.990
Joe's the manager of
our Google alliance.

00:21:40.990 --> 00:21:42.020
We've got other
folks down there.

00:21:42.020 --> 00:21:43.394
Feel free to come
by, get a demo,

00:21:43.394 --> 00:21:49.638
or just sort of learn a
little more about Smartsheet.

00:21:49.638 --> 00:21:51.590
And there's-- thank you.

00:21:51.590 --> 00:21:56.474
And I'm handing it
off to ProsperWorks.

